def _normalize_role(message: BaseMessage) -> str | None:
    for message_class, role in _ROLE_BY_CLASS:
        if isinstance(message, message_class):
            return role.value
    return None
```
Returning `str | None` lets callers apply context-specific defaults (e.g. `_normalize_role(msg) or "user"` for input messages vs `or "assistant"` for output messages) instead of falling back to `message.type` which leaks LangChain AST type names like `"chat"` or `"remove"`.
